1
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:02,960
Kew Gardens, Queens,

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,800
March 13, 1964,

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,890
a little after three in the morning.

4
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:13,050
A red Fiat turns into the parking

5
00:00:13,090 --> 00:00:16,090
lot beside the Kew Gardens train station.

6
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:20,180
Behind the wheel is 28-year-old

7
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:22,150
Catherine Genovese.

8
00:00:22,190 --> 00:00:24,150
Everyone calls her Kitty.

9
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,520
She has just closed up

10
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:28,140
the bar she manages in Hollis.

11
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:29,560
Her apartment is less

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,710
than a hundred feet away.

13
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:33,570
She doesn't notice the white

14
00:00:33,610 --> 00:00:35,750
car that has been following her.

15
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:38,750
It stops at the curb just behind her.

16
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:41,510
Winston Moseley would later tell

17
00:00:41,550 --> 00:00:44,620
police he left home that night for one reason,

18
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:47,170
to find a woman and kill her.

19
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,330
Kitty starts walking.

20
00:00:49,370 --> 00:00:51,720
Behind her, a car door opens.

21
00:00:52,570 --> 00:00:54,140
Halfway to her door,

22
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,170
she sees him,

23
00:00:55,210 --> 00:00:56,370
and she runs.

24
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:06,650
Across Austin Street,

25
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:08,690
the lights started coming on.

26
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:10,890
Dozens of people heard her,

27
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:12,790
some went to their windows.

28
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:15,090
What they did next would haunt

29
00:01:15,130 --> 00:01:17,530
this city for the next 60 years.

30
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,632
Catherine Susan Genovese

31
00:01:32,672 --> 00:01:35,472
was born in Brooklyn on July 7,

32
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:40,115
1935, the eldest of five children

33
00:01:40,155 --> 00:01:42,090
in an Italian-American family.

34
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,610
Everyone called her Kitty.

35
00:01:44,650 --> 00:01:46,970
Friends remembered her as outgoing,

36
00:01:47,010 --> 00:01:48,110
quick to laugh,

37
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:50,260
and fiercely independent.

38
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,890
When her family moved to Connecticut,

39
00:01:52,930 --> 00:01:54,550
Kitty stayed behind.

40
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:56,280
New York was home.

41
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:01,716
By 1964, she was managing

42
00:02:01,756 --> 00:02:03,297
Ev's Eleventh Hour,

43
00:02:03,337 --> 00:02:04,776
a bar in Hollis,

44
00:02:04,816 --> 00:02:05,208
Queens.

45
00:02:05,248 --> 00:02:06,163
She worked late,

46
00:02:06,203 --> 00:02:08,168
she knew the regulars by name,

47
00:02:08,208 --> 00:02:09,936
and she was saving her money.

48
00:02:09,976 --> 00:02:10,985
She dreamed of one day

49
00:02:11,025 --> 00:02:13,170
opening a restaurant of her own.

50
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,343
She shared a small apartment

51
00:02:15,383 --> 00:02:17,308
in Kew Gardens with her partner,

52
00:02:17,348 --> 00:02:19,095
Mary Ann Zielonko.

53
00:02:19,135 --> 00:02:22,315
In 1964, two women could

54
00:02:22,355 --> 00:02:24,271
not live openly as a couple.

55
00:02:24,311 --> 00:02:25,158
To the neighbors,

56
00:02:25,198 --> 00:02:26,940
they were simply roommates.

57
00:02:28,510 --> 00:02:30,526
On the night of March 12,

58
00:02:30,566 --> 00:02:32,537
Kitty worked until closing.

59
00:02:32,577 --> 00:02:35,162
A little after 2:30 in the morning,

60
00:02:35,202 --> 00:02:35,969
she locked up,

61
00:02:36,009 --> 00:02:37,450
said goodnight, and got

62
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:39,280
into her little red Fiat.

63
00:02:40,870 --> 00:02:42,850
Somewhere along the way home,

64
00:02:42,890 --> 00:02:45,780
a man in a white Corvair noticed her car.

65
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:48,590
He followed it all the way to Kew Gardens.

66
00:02:58,420 --> 00:02:59,920
Across Austin Street,

67
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,700
a light snapped on.

68
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:04,160
From his window in the Mowbray apartments,

69
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:06,790
Robert Mozer shouted into the dark.

70
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:09,600
Let that girl alone!

71
00:03:11,910 --> 00:03:13,670
The man ran back to his car

72
00:03:13,710 --> 00:03:15,400
and drove away.

73
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:18,430
Kitty was alive.

74
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:20,520
Badly wounded, she got to her feet

75
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:23,010
and stumbled along the side of the building,

76
00:03:23,050 --> 00:03:24,480
toward the back entrance,

77
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,500
out of sight of the street.

78
00:03:27,090 --> 00:03:27,970
For a few minutes,

79
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:30,370
Austin Street went quiet again.

80
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:31,730
Lights went out.

81
00:03:31,770 --> 00:03:33,170
Some neighbors later said

82
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:34,680
they thought it was a drunk,

83
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:36,460
or a lovers' quarrel.

84
00:03:38,410 --> 00:03:39,990
About ten minutes later,

85
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:41,970
the white Corvair came back.

86
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,617
Moseley searched the parking lot,

87
00:03:45,657 --> 00:03:46,911
the train station,

88
00:03:46,951 --> 00:03:48,087
the street.

89
00:03:48,127 --> 00:03:49,727
He found her in a small vestibule

90
00:03:49,767 --> 00:03:51,510
at the back of her building,

91
00:03:51,550 --> 00:03:53,690
just a few feet from her own door.

92
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,026
There, he attacked her again.

93
00:03:57,066 --> 00:03:57,973
He stabbed her,

94
00:03:58,013 --> 00:03:59,594
sexually assaulted her,

95
00:03:59,634 --> 00:04:02,920
and took $49 from her wallet.

96
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,010
At the top of the stairs,

97
00:04:07,050 --> 00:04:08,180
a neighbor named Karl

98
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:10,170
Ross opened his door.

99
00:04:10,210 --> 00:04:11,460
He saw what was happening.

100
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:13,230
And he closed it again.

101
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,820
Instead of calling the police,

102
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:17,900
he called a friend for advice.

103
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:19,820
Later, he would explain:

104
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:21,620
I didn't want to get involved.

105
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:26,370
Sophia Farrar didn't hesitate.

106
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:28,100
She ran out of her apartment

107
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:29,790
and down to the vestibule,

108
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:30,900
not knowing whether

109
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:32,670
the killer was still there.

110
00:04:32,710 --> 00:04:33,780
She found Kitty,

111
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:36,060
and held her in her arms.

112
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:39,561
The police were finally called

113
00:04:39,601 --> 00:04:42,290
at about 3:50 in the morning.

114
00:04:42,330 --> 00:04:44,170
They arrived within minutes.

115
00:04:46,250 --> 00:04:48,705
Kitty Genovese died in the ambulance

116
00:04:48,745 --> 00:04:50,759
on the way to the hospital.

117
00:04:50,799 --> 00:04:53,300
She was 28 years old.

118
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:05,681
Five days later,

119
00:05:05,721 --> 00:05:07,726
in Corona, Queens,

120
00:05:07,766 --> 00:05:09,969
a resident named Raoul Cleary

121
00:05:10,009 --> 00:05:11,903
noticed a stranger carrying

122
00:05:11,943 --> 00:05:14,582
a television set out of a neighbor's house,

123
00:05:14,622 --> 00:05:16,370
in broad daylight.

124
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:18,720
The man said he was helping

125
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:19,900
the family move.

126
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,650
Cleary didn't believe him.

127
00:05:21,690 --> 00:05:22,810
While they talked,

128
00:05:22,850 --> 00:05:24,930
another neighbor, Jack Brown,

129
00:05:24,970 --> 00:05:27,680
quietly disabled the stranger's car.

130
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:29,560
When the police arrived,

131
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,340
the man was arrested.

132
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:33,990
His name was Winston Moseley.

133
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:37,670
In custody, Moseley confessed,

134
00:05:37,710 --> 00:05:39,182
calmly and in detail,

135
00:05:39,222 --> 00:05:41,661
to the murder of Kitty Genovese.

136
00:05:41,701 --> 00:05:43,227
And then to two more.

137
00:05:43,267 --> 00:05:44,572
Annie Mae Johnson.

138
00:05:44,612 --> 00:05:46,320
And Barbara Kralik.

139
00:05:48,130 --> 00:05:50,418
He was 29 years old.

140
00:05:50,458 --> 00:05:51,670
A married father,

141
00:05:51,710 --> 00:05:54,810
with a steady job and no criminal record.

142
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:56,719
Asked why, he told detectives

143
00:05:56,759 --> 00:05:58,420
he had an urge to kill.

144
00:06:07,230 --> 00:06:08,770
Two weeks after the murder,

145
00:06:08,810 --> 00:06:11,490
the city editor of The New York Times,

146
00:06:11,530 --> 00:06:11,820
A.

147
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:12,150
M.

148
00:06:12,190 --> 00:06:14,100
Rosenthal, had lunch with Police

149
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:15,920
Commissioner Michael Murphy.

150
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:18,520
Murphy brought up the Genovese case.

151
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:19,760
One detail, he said,

152
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,690
had stayed with him.

153
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:25,677
On March 27, the Times

154
00:06:25,717 --> 00:06:28,020
ran the story on its front page.

155
00:06:29,250 --> 00:06:33,163
38 respectable, law-abiding citizens,

156
00:06:33,203 --> 00:06:35,169
it said, had watched a killer stalk

157
00:06:35,209 --> 00:06:37,865
and stab a woman in three separate attacks,

158
00:06:37,905 --> 00:06:39,713
over more than half an hour.

159
00:06:39,753 --> 00:06:42,260
And not one of them had called the police.

160
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:45,960
The story exploded.

161
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,720
It was read on the radio,

162
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:49,160
preached from pulpits,

163
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,320
debated across the country.

164
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:53,320
Kitty Genovese became a symbol

165
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:55,820
of a city where nobody cared.

166
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:01,707
In 1968, two psychologists,

167
00:07:01,747 --> 00:07:03,453
John Darley and Bibb Latané,

168
00:07:03,493 --> 00:07:05,600
set out to test the idea.

169
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:08,017
Students sat alone in small booths,

170
00:07:08,057 --> 00:07:09,698
talking over an intercom,

171
00:07:09,738 --> 00:07:10,648
when one of them appeared

172
00:07:10,688 --> 00:07:11,880
to have a seizure.

173
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:13,428
When a student believed

174
00:07:13,468 --> 00:07:15,090
they were the only one listening,

175
00:07:15,130 --> 00:07:18,037
85% went for help.

176
00:07:18,077 --> 00:07:19,275
When they believed four

177
00:07:19,315 --> 00:07:20,422
others could hear it too,

178
00:07:20,462 --> 00:07:23,370
only 31% did.

179
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:27,660
They called it the bystander effect.

180
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:30,200
The more people who witness an emergency,

181
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:33,390
the less likely any one of them is to act.

182
00:07:42,130 --> 00:07:43,580
But when researchers,

183
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:44,940
journalists and lawyers

184
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:46,730
went back to the evidence,

185
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:49,070
the story began to fall apart.

186
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:51,666
The first attack happened

187
00:07:51,706 --> 00:07:53,774
at 3:19 in the morning,

188
00:07:53,814 --> 00:07:56,493
in March, with most windows shut.

189
00:07:56,533 --> 00:07:58,392
Many neighbors heard something.

190
00:07:58,432 --> 00:08:00,744
Very few saw anything clearly.

191
00:08:00,784 --> 00:08:02,409
Several thought it was a drunk,

192
00:08:02,449 --> 00:08:04,090
or a couple fighting.

193
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,680
The second attack,

194
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,720
the fatal one,

195
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:09,260
happened inside the vestibule.

196
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:09,900
From the street,

197
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:11,720
and from almost every window,

198
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,230
it was invisible.

199
00:08:15,070 --> 00:08:17,241
At least one man shouted from his window,

200
00:08:17,281 --> 00:08:19,626
and drove the attacker off.

201
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:20,525
At least one,

202
00:08:20,565 --> 00:08:22,320
and possibly two people,

203
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:25,181
called the police after the first attack.

204
00:08:25,221 --> 00:08:26,784
And Sophia Farrar went

205
00:08:26,824 --> 00:08:29,470
down and held Kitty as she died.

206
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:35,656
In 2007, psychologists Rachel Manning,

207
00:08:35,696 --> 00:08:37,443
Mark Levine and Alan Collins

208
00:08:37,483 --> 00:08:39,408
concluded there was no evidence

209
00:08:39,448 --> 00:08:43,170
that 38 people had watched and done nothing.

210
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:47,393
In 2016, The New York Times itself

211
00:08:47,433 --> 00:08:49,548
acknowledged that its story had

212
00:08:49,588 --> 00:08:52,659
grossly exaggerated the number of witnesses,

213
00:08:52,699 --> 00:08:54,250
and what they had seen.

214
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:57,097
Kitty's younger brother,

215
00:08:57,137 --> 00:08:59,745
Bill Genovese, spent years tracking

216
00:08:59,785 --> 00:09:01,364
down the people who were there that night.

217
00:09:01,404 --> 00:09:03,318
His film, The Witness,

218
00:09:03,358 --> 00:09:06,730
was released in 2015.

219
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:18,065
In June 1964,

220
00:09:18,105 --> 00:09:19,842
Winston Moseley was convicted

221
00:09:19,882 --> 00:09:22,856
of murder and sentenced to death.

222
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:24,238
On appeal, his sentence

223
00:09:24,278 --> 00:09:26,400
was reduced to life in prison.

224
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:31,461
In 1968, during a hospital

225
00:09:31,501 --> 00:09:32,609
trip in Buffalo,

226
00:09:32,649 --> 00:09:35,480
he overpowered a guard and escaped.

227
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:37,291
He took hostages and assaulted

228
00:09:37,331 --> 00:09:39,690
a woman before he was captured again.

229
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:43,829
He was denied parole 18 times.

230
00:09:43,869 --> 00:09:46,601
He died in prison on March 28,

231
00:09:46,641 --> 00:09:50,316
2016, at the age of 81.

232
00:09:50,356 --> 00:09:53,130
He outlived Kitty by 52 years.

233
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,083
The 38 witnesses were,

234
00:09:58,123 --> 00:09:59,714
in large part,

235
00:09:59,754 --> 00:10:00,143
a myth.

236
00:10:00,183 --> 00:10:02,660
But the question the story asked was real,

237
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:04,530
and it has never gone away.

238
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,780
When you hear someone scream in the night,

239
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:10,620
when you're not sure what it is,

240
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:13,000
and you're not sure anyone else will help,

241
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,230
what do you do?

